    prepTime: 30,
    recordTime: 40,
    difficulty: "hard",
    content: {
      text: "Regenerative medicine aims to repair or replace damaged tissues and organs through stem cell therapy, tissue engineering, and molecular biology techniques. While significant progress has been made in laboratory settings, clinical applications face challenges including immune rejection, ethical concerns, and regulatory hurdles that slow translation from research to treatment."
    }
