    title: "Read Aloud",
    instruction: "Read the text aloud as naturally as possible. You have 30 seconds to prepare.",
    prepTime: 30,
    recordTime: 40,
    difficulty: "hard",
    content: {
      text: "The sociology of science investigates how social factors influence the production and validation of scientific knowledge. Peer review, funding structures, and institutional hierarchies all shape which research gets conducted and accepted. Feminist and postcolonial scholars have highlighted how dominant perspectives can marginalize alternative ways of knowing. Understanding science as a social activity does not diminish its achievements but provides a more complete picture of how knowledge develops."
    }
