    title: "Summarize Group Discussion",
    instruction: "Listen once to the 2–3 minute group discussion. You have 10 seconds to prepare and up to 2 minutes to summarize the main points.",
    prepTime: 10,
    recordTime: 120,
    difficulty: "easy",
    content: {
      discussionContent: "Moderator: We are here to discuss social equity. Let's explore the key issues and potential approaches.\nSpeaker A: I believe equal opportunity should be our priority. It addresses the immediate needs while laying the groundwork for diversity inclusion. We need to consider both short-term and long-term perspectives.\nSpeaker B: I agree, but we also need to think about community support. Without addressing this, our efforts may not be sustainable. We should look at what has worked in other contexts.\nModerator: What are your thoughts on the resources required for these initiatives?\nSpeaker A: Investment in policy reform is essential, though we should be realistic about budget constraints. A phased approach might be more practical than trying to do everything at once.\nSpeaker B: We should also consider resource distribution as a way to build momentum. If people can see early results, they are more likely to support continued efforts. Communication is key.\nModerator: How do we measure whether these efforts are successful?\nSpeaker A: We need clear indicators related to social justice. Regular monitoring and evaluation will help us understand what is working and what needs adjustment.\nSpeaker B: I also suggest involving the community in the evaluation process. Their feedback is invaluable and ensures that our efforts are responsive to actual needs rather than assumptions.\nModerator: So the group recommends focusing on equal opportunity, diversity inclusion, and community support, with investment in policy reform and resource distribution, and clear metrics around social justice. We will develop a detailed plan and timeline for moving forward."
    }
